	1. Run log re use wait 
SELECT name, log_reuse_wait_desc FROM sys.databases 

If you have replication holds

	2.  EXEC sp_repltrans  (against database)

Results set will look like 
xdesid			               xact_seqno
0x0000171B000089500001	0x0000171B000089AC0001
0x0000171B00008A770001	0x0000171B00008A980001
0x0000185F0003C16A0001	0x0000185F0003C1DC0001
0x000019A90002C4A00001	0x000019A90002C59F0001

	3.  EXEC sp_repldone @xactid = 0x000019A90002C4A00001, @xact_segno = NULL, @numtrans = 0, @TIME = 0, @EGCC = 1 
(put each xdesid from step 2 in the @xactid = 0x000019A90002C4A00001 ) --run it for all the xdesid one by one against each database

	4. Take log backup of the database and shrink (may need to do it a few times)

	5. optional
EXEC sp_changepublication
@Publication='DW_CP_Pub',
@Property=N'replicate_ddl',
@value=0

Finally run log reuse wait again to verify 
